From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:24:09 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 14/17] wifi: b43: serialize A-MPDU TX session
 state with wl->mutex

b43_op_ampdu_action() updates the per-TID A-MPDU state (ampdu_buf,
ampdu_nssn, ampdu_bar_ssn) and the per-station limits (ampdu_max_len,
ampdu_density) without holding wl->mutex. b43_tx_work() reads that state
while it builds aggregates, and the TX status path reads it to send
BARs. Both run under wl->mutex. A session starting or stopping can
therefore change the state in the middle of building an aggregate or
handling a status.

mac80211 calls the ampdu_action callback from sleepable context, so take
wl->mutex around the TX_OPERATIONAL and TX_STOP_* updates. Call
ieee80211_stop_tx_ba_cb_irqsafe() after dropping the mutex, as before.

This locking only makes each update atomic against those readers. It
does not drain the frames or statuses of a stopped session that are
still queued or in flight, and it does not tag them with a session
epoch. A status from an old session can still be processed against the
state of a new session on the same TID. That is a separate problem and
is not addressed here.

Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
index 486893cdc326..2b67e9dde62f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -5649,6 +5649,13 @@ static int b43_op_ampdu_action(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	struct b43_wl *wl = hw_to_b43_wl(hw);
 	struct ieee80211_sta *sta = params->sta;
 
+	/* The per-TID session state below is read by b43_tx_work() and the
+	 * TX status path, both under wl->mutex. This callback may sleep, so
+	 * take the mutex for the updates. It only keeps each update atomic
+	 * against those readers: frames and statuses of a stopped session
+	 * that are still in flight are not drained or told apart from a new
+	 * session on the same TID.
+	 */
 	switch (params->action) {
 	case IEEE80211_AMPDU_RX_START:
 	case IEEE80211_AMPDU_RX_STOP:
@@ -5658,17 +5665,21 @@ static int b43_op_ampdu_action(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 		return IEEE80211_AMPDU_TX_START_IMMEDIATE;
 	case IEEE80211_AMPDU_TX_OPERATIONAL:
+		mutex_lock(&wl->mutex);
 		wl->ampdu_nssn[params->tid] = 0;
 		wl->ampdu_bar_ssn[params->tid] = 0;
 		wl->ampdu_max_len = (1 << (IEEE80211_HT_MAX_AMPDU_FACTOR +
 					   sta->deflink.ht_cap.ampdu_factor)) - 1;
 		wl->ampdu_density = sta->deflink.ht_cap.ampdu_density;
 		wl->ampdu_buf[params->tid] = min_t(u16, params->buf_size, 64);
+		mutex_unlock(&wl->mutex);
 		return 0;
 	case IEEE80211_AMPDU_TX_STOP_CONT:
 	case IEEE80211_AMPDU_TX_STOP_FLUSH:
 	case IEEE80211_AMPDU_TX_STOP_FLUSH_CONT:
+		mutex_lock(&wl->mutex);
 		wl->ampdu_buf[params->tid] = 0;
+		mutex_unlock(&wl->mutex);
 		ieee80211_stop_tx_ba_cb_irqsafe(vif, sta->addr, params->tid);
 		return 0;
 	default:
